1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
What could your Python change affect?

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,800
Compare two commits from a GitHub repository.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,000
Loading pauses shortened.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Start with one changed function.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
A test may call the changed health function.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Select the test to highlight its connection.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Inspect its file and version. ImpactLens has not run this test.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Choose another change to explore its callers.

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Focus on one connection.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Bring other connections back into view.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
Next, compare a change that deletes a function.

12
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Deleted code uses connections from the older version.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Follow a focused path to the former POST /analyze route.

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:57,000
These are older-version dependencies. They may no longer exist.

15
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Finally, compare a change that only adds the README.

16
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
No Python code changed, so there is no Python change to trace.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Dynamic calls can be missed. Review code and run tests.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Use the map to guide your review.
